the-firm-as-one-program-24 : List Word
the-firm-as-one-program-24 = unlines (cons "- **C1** Prove any provable property of the whole firm ([P2: Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (hyperactivity v31 §1–2)], [P6: Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)], [P7: One evaluator realizes everything, through C (hyperactivity v31 §9)])." (cons "  A firm built as one program can ask any question about itself and receive a proof in place of an estimate. Whether any sequence of exchange events, across every strategy and gateway, can push exposure in a name past its limit is a type over the composed fleet. Today such questions are answered by sampling: tests, simulations, monitoring and post-mortems. In one program they are answered for every run at once." nil))
